  "method": "KRAB vs non-KRAB was decided in bulk from UniProt rather than gene by gene. I streamed every human protein carrying the KRAB domain under four independent signatures - Pfam PF01352, InterPro IPR001909, PROSITE PRU00119/PS50805 and SMART SM00349 - via the UniProt REST API (rest.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/stream, organism_id:9606), giving a union of 429 KRAB-domain gene symbols; 288 of the 390 input symbols fell inside it and were assigned KRAB_ZNF. For the 102 that did not, I pulled reviewed UniProt records with fields gene_primary, protein_name, ft_domain, cc_similarity and cc_caution, then downloaded their sequences and regex-scanned the N-terminal 130 aa for the canonical KRAB A-box (LVTFxDVAVxFSxEEW-like). That recovered four curator-annotated or degenerate KRABs the signature databases missed (ZNF324A/ZNF324, ZNF705E/ZNF705EP, ZNF788/ZNF788P, ZNF774) and confirmed the rest as KRAB-free, including several - ZNF134, ZNF329, ZNF345, ZNF35 - that the literature loosely calls KZFPs. The same ft_domain pass supplied the non-KRAB sub-calls: SCAN box without KRAB to ZSCAN (ZNF165, ZNF174, ZNF232, ZNF396, ZNF444, ZNF449), BTB to ZBTB_OTHER (ZNF131, whose UniProt symbol is ZBTB35), ZAD/no-domain to ZNF_OTHER. Dedicated keys were applied first and override the domain call: ZNF143/ZNF76, ZNF263, ZNF281/ZNF148, ZNF24, ZNF384 (+ZNF362), ZNF410, ZNF460 (+ZNF317, since that entry is named 'ZNF460 / ZNF317-like'), ZNF768, ZFP57 (ZNF445) and ZFP_TE (ZNF93, ZNF808, ZNF780A). Note that UniProt contradicts the caller's 'notable non-KRAB' hint list for ZNF101, ZNF202 (ZKSCAN10, KRAB+SCAN), ZNF212, ZNF282, ZNF287, ZNF300, ZNF317, ZNF350, ZNF707, ZNF777, ZNF778, ZNF785, ZNF786 and ZNF792, all of which do carry a KRAB domain and were therefore assigned KRAB_ZNF (or their dedicated key); I followed the database over the hint and flagged the debatable ones. Nine network fetches were used in total."
}
